  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/moenkhausia-phaeonota-4/",
      "html": "<p>This small (about 4 cm) species of tetra originates from the upper Rio Tapajós basin in the Mato Grosso state in Brazil. It is the only species of Moenkhausia with such a colour pattern.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/moenkhausia-phaeonota-4/",
      "html": "<p>Upper Rio Tapajós basin, Mato Grosso state, Brazil.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/moenkhausia-phaeonota-4/",
      "html": "<p>If one observes the live fish, the behaviour is reminiscent of croaking tetras (Stevardiinae).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/moenkhausia-phaeonota-4/",
      "html": "<p>In the original scientific description (1979), the author already mentioned that the generic placement could only be provisional. This provisional placement still stands today for Moenkhausia phaeonota. Sadly, this charming tetra is only very rarely available.</p>"
    }
